{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Which of the nine gems to wear, from the sidereal lagna. Two schools are implemented: `lagna-lord` (default) prescribes the gems of the 1st, 9th and 5th lords as the life, lucky and benefic stones; `functional-benefic` classifies every graha by the houses it owns from the lagna, prescribes only for functional benefics led by the yogakaraka, and names the functional malefics as gems to avoid.\n\n[Group: Vedic]\n[Endpoint: POST /v1/vedic/gemstones]\n[Cost: 20 credits (Tier 2)]","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"body":{"allOf":[{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}]},"description":"Birth data for a single natal chart. Required: date (YYYY-MM-DD), time (HH:mm:ss), latitude and longitude in decimal degrees. The short forms lat, lon, lng and tz are rejected with 400 INVALID_FIELD; pass the full names. timezoneOffset is hours from UTC and defaults to 0, meaning UTC; send timezone instead (an IANA name such as Europe/Kyiv, or auto) and the offset for that date is worked out, summer time included. city is a display label only: nothing here geocodes it, so it never stands in for coordinates. houseSystem is a single house-system letter, P by default; a name such as \"Placidus\" is refused, and the case matters because I and i are two different Sunshine systems.","properties":{"ayanamsa":{"description":"Sidereal school by name. Lahiri when omitted. Equivalent to ayanamsaId; send either.","enum":["fagan-bradley","lahiri","de-luce","raman","krishnamurti","kp","yukteshwar","jn-bhasin","true-citra","djwhal-khul"],"type":"string"},"ayanamsaId":{"type":["number","null"]},"city":{"default":"","type":"string"},"cosmogram":{"type":"boolean"},"date":{"pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"},"houseSystem":{"default":"P","enum":["P","K","R","C","E","W","B","M","O","A","T","V","D","F","G","H","I","i","L","N","Q","S","U","X","Y"],"type":"string"},"latitude":{"maximum":90,"minimum":-90,"type":"number"},"longitude":{"maximum":180,"minimum":-180,"type":"number"},"name":{"default":"","type":"string"},"time":{"pattern":"^\\d{2}:\\d{2}(:\\d{2})?$","type":"string"},"timezone":{"description":"IANA zone name such as Europe/Kyiv, or auto to look the zone up from latitude and longitude. The server takes the offset that zone kept at this local date and time, summer time included, and uses it in place of timezoneOffset. A clock time that happened twice takes the first occurrence; one skipped when clocks went forward takes the offset from before the change. Abbreviations such as EST are refused. Before 1970 the tz database is not reliable for every place, so send timezoneOffset when the local clock is known.","type":"string"},"timezoneOffset":{"anyOf":[{"maximum":14,"minimum":-14,"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":0,"description":"Hours from UTC at the given moment, not minutes. Fractional zones are hours too: 5.5 for India, 5.75 for Nepal, -3.5 for Newfoundland. Defaults to 0, meaning UTC. Ignored when timezone is sent."},"zodiacType":{"enum":["tropical","sidereal"],"type":"string"}},"required":["date","time","latitude","longitude"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}]},"properties":{"latitude":{"description":"Birth latitude. Required: the lagna is what both schools prescribe from.","maximum":90,"minimum":-90,"type":"number"},"longitude":{"description":"Birth longitude. Required: the lagna is what both schools prescribe from.","maximum":180,"minimum":-180,"type":"number"},"school":{"description":"Prescription school. Both reach the same three gems (the trikona lords), and differ on what they withhold and on the ordering. The response always names the one used. Default: lagna-lord.","enum":["lagna-lord","functional-benefic"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"}],"description":"Birth data for a gemstone recommendation. Required: date (YYYY-MM-DD), time (HH:mm:ss), latitude and longitude. Coordinates do NOT default to 0 here as they do on other chart endpoints: the whole answer is derived from the lagna, so an omitted pair is a 400 rather than a confident set of gems for 0N 0E."}},"required":["body"],"type":"object"},"name":"astroway_vedic_gemstones","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}]},"properties":{"avoid":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}]},"properties":{"basis":{"type":["string","null"]},"gem":{"type":["string","null"]},"gemSanskrit":{"type":["string","null"]},"graha":{"type":["number","null"]},"grahaName":{"type":["string","null"]},"grahaSanskrit":{"type":["string","null"]},"housesOwned":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":["number","null"]},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]},"mineral":{"type":["string","null"]},"role":{"type":["string","null"]},"substitutes":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":["string","null"]},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]},"wearing":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}]},"properties":{"day":{"type":["string","null"]},"finger":{"type":["string","null"]},"fingerVariants":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":["string","null"]},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]},"japaCount":{"type":["number","null"]},"mantra":{"type":["string","null"]},"metals":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":["string","null"]},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]},"minWeight":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}]},"properties":{"carats":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":["number","null"]},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]},"grams":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":["number","null"]},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]},"ratti":{"anyOf":[{"items":{"type":["number","null"]},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]}},"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}]}},"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}]}},"type":"object"},{"type":"null"}]},"type":"array"},{"type":"null"